            <div xml:id="d132-a1">

                <pb facs="0417" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg369"/>

                <p rendition="#center">PROTOCOL.</p>
                <p>The undersigned, Reverdy Johnson, esq., envoy extraordinary and minister
                    plenipotentiary of the United States of America, and Edward Henry, Lord Stanley,
                    her Britannic Majesty’s principal secretary of state for foreign affairs, being
                    respectively authorized and empowered by their governments, hereby declare that
                    the said governments agree to refer the disputed question of boundary, which
                    forms the subject of the protocol signed by them on the 17th of October last, to
                    the decision of the President of the federal council of the Swiss
                    confederation.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Done at <placeName>London</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-11-10">the 10th of November,
                            1868</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>REVERDY JOHNSON.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>STANLEY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
